WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:08.090 --> 00:00:11.500
Okay, before we get started today, I must
give you two warnings:

00:00:11.500 --> 00:00:14.980
The first one is that we might include some
spoilers about Narcos, obviously.

00:00:14.980 --> 00:00:19.150
But, given that this is a TV show based on
real history, I don’t think this is that

00:00:19.150 --> 00:00:20.150
much a problem.

00:00:20.150 --> 00:00:23.340
The second warning is that today we are going
to talk about drug trafficking...

00:00:23.340 --> 00:00:27.900
A topic where the information we have is incomplete
and, at all the time police are finding new

00:00:27.900 --> 00:00:32.960
bits of information that could prove parts
of this video wrong.

00:00:32.960 --> 00:00:37.230
This being said…

00:00:37.230 --> 00:00:42.320
Colombia is known as the “country of a thousand
rhythms”, the country of coffee.

00:00:42.320 --> 00:00:46.890
and the birthplace of many of those latino
singers that got the whole world to dance...

00:00:46.890 --> 00:00:54.110
Nevertheless, what really made this country
famous is, sadly, this man…

00:00:54.110 --> 00:00:57.079
The king of cocaine.

00:00:57.079 --> 00:01:00.510
The man who basically created one of the world’s
most dangerous industries…

00:01:00.510 --> 00:01:04.830
At the end of the 1980s, Pablo Escobar, or
‘EL PATRON´, as his neighbours used to

00:01:04.830 --> 00:01:09.509
know him, controlled 90% of the worldwide
production of cocaine.

00:01:09.509 --> 00:01:14.259
Suddenly, Medellin, a city of 2 million inhabitants,
became the Hollywood of cocaine.

00:01:14.259 --> 00:01:19.459
However, on December the first, 1993, he died
during a shootout with the police.

00:01:19.459 --> 00:01:21.860
But you probably already knew that...

00:01:21.860 --> 00:01:24.600
So the question now becomes: What happened
after?

00:01:24.600 --> 00:01:26.890
Who took Pablo Escobar’s business?

00:01:26.890 --> 00:01:30.180
And then there is the most important question
of all…

00:01:30.180 --> 00:01:32.970
Is there still cocaine trafficking in Colombia?

00:01:32.970 --> 00:01:37.789
Well, today, we are gonna answer all of those
questions… but before we get into all of

00:01:37.789 --> 00:01:46.759
that, let’s talk a little bit about cocaine…

00:01:46.759 --> 00:01:50.250
After weed, cocaine is the second most consumed
drug in the world.

00:01:50.250 --> 00:01:54.000
But, unlike the first one, cocaine is extremely
hard to find.

00:01:54.000 --> 00:01:58.460
Marijuana grows anywhere on the planet - even
in cold places like North America.

00:01:58.460 --> 00:02:03.480
Grow houses are found all the time… with
just a little bit of expenditure, anyone can

00:02:03.480 --> 00:02:07.090
create, at home, the optimal conditions for
growing cannabis.

00:02:07.090 --> 00:02:09.739
But coca leaves are a different animal.

00:02:09.739 --> 00:02:12.959
You need a very specific habitat.

00:02:12.959 --> 00:02:15.980
This is why only some countries can grow it.

00:02:15.980 --> 00:02:18.640
The main ones are Colombia, Peru and Bolivia...

00:02:18.640 --> 00:02:31.069
In other words, there is space for just a
few suppliers but the demand won’t stop

00:02:31.069 --> 00:02:34.459
growing - and it’s a global demand.

00:02:34.459 --> 00:02:38.969
This is why cocaine is such a high profit
business, and this is why, right after Pablo

00:02:38.969 --> 00:02:46.450
Escobar’s death, there were lots of people
willing to take his place.

00:02:46.450 --> 00:02:47.510
MAFIA WARS

00:02:47.510 --> 00:02:50.890
As you know, Pablo Escobar was the leader
of the Medellin cartel.

00:02:50.890 --> 00:02:55.560
But, even before his death, there was already
a second cocaine capital, and this was the

00:02:55.560 --> 00:03:06.599
city of CALI, also in Colombia and with very
similar population.

00:03:06.599 --> 00:03:38.409
The 

00:03:38.409 --> 00:03:41.879
Cali cartel wanted to take the whole of Pablo
Escobar’s business.

00:03:41.879 --> 00:03:45.530
But Medellin had plenty of narcos wanting
to do the same thing.

00:03:45.530 --> 00:03:48.290
One of them was DIEGO FERNANDEZ MURILLO, A.K.A.

00:03:48.290 --> 00:03:49.290
Don Berna.

00:03:49.290 --> 00:03:58.510
Don Berna helped the police deal with Pablo
Escobar, made an alliance with the Cali Cartel,

00:03:58.510 --> 00:04:03.370
and even had close ties with a right-wing
paramilitary group called the Colombian Self

00:04:03.370 --> 00:04:04.370
Defense Forces.

00:04:04.370 --> 00:04:08.690
With Pablo Escobar dead and buried, Don Berna
started a new organization with this paramilitary

00:04:08.690 --> 00:04:10.450
group, the so-called OFICINA DE ENVIGADO.

00:04:10.450 --> 00:04:15.909
At the same time, all the little Narcos in
Medellin where also fighting for their share

00:04:15.909 --> 00:04:16.909
of the cake.

00:04:16.909 --> 00:04:21.780
This street you see here was the border between
one band and the other.

00:04:21.780 --> 00:04:28.919
Basically, if you were a worker for the OFICINA
DE ENVIGADO and crossed this street, someone

00:04:28.919 --> 00:04:30.370
would kill you immediately.

00:04:30.370 --> 00:04:35.169
So, as you can imagine, these were extremely
violent times for the city - different drug

00:04:35.169 --> 00:04:37.930
bands were killing each other all the time.

00:04:37.930 --> 00:04:41.090
Meanwhile, the Cali cartel was way more subtle...

00:04:41.090 --> 00:04:44.800
This is GILBERTO RODRIGUEZ and his partner,
PACHO HERRERA.

00:04:44.800 --> 00:04:48.949
They were high class boys, with plenty of
contacts among politicians and judges.

00:04:48.949 --> 00:04:54.389
In fact, Gilberto Rodriguez paid over $6 million
to finance the campaign of one of the Colombian

00:04:54.389 --> 00:04:56.240
presidents, Ernesto Samper.

00:04:56.240 --> 00:05:00.330
Nonetheless, despite the influence and the
corruption, after sometime the inevitable

00:05:00.330 --> 00:05:02.270
happened…

00:05:02.270 --> 00:05:10.490
‘The government has started the extradition
process for the chief of the Cali Cartel’

00:05:10.490 --> 00:05:14.210
Nonetheless, Don Berna, violent as he was,
had a totally different story.

00:05:14.210 --> 00:05:18.139
Actually, among all the characters that appear
on the Narcos TV show, Don Berna is the one

00:05:18.139 --> 00:05:21.569
who has lasted the longest without being put
behind bars.

00:05:21.569 --> 00:05:24.460
But… wait just a minute because now we are
going to talk about the characters that didn’t

00:05:24.460 --> 00:05:25.460
appear on the show!

00:05:25.460 --> 00:05:27.030
At least, in the first two seasons!

00:05:27.030 --> 00:05:29.870
And… prepare yourself because there is a
lot to tell.

00:05:29.870 --> 00:05:32.870
Do you remember how Don Berna worked with
this right wing group?

00:05:32.870 --> 00:05:36.940
Well… the political ideology was more important
than what you might think.

00:05:36.940 --> 00:05:43.100
The Colombian Self Defenses Forces were born
to fight against communist guerrillas in the

00:05:43.100 --> 00:05:44.100
country…

00:05:44.100 --> 00:05:49.080
FUERZAS ARMADAS REVOLUCIONARIAS DE COLOMBIA
- FARC

00:05:49.080 --> 00:05:52.300
FARC is more than a simple terrorist group.

00:05:52.300 --> 00:05:55.920
In some areas of the country, they became
a parallel government.

00:05:55.920 --> 00:05:59.590
More than an Al Qaeda kind of thing, they
could better be compared with DAESH, or Islamic

00:05:59.590 --> 00:06:00.590
State.

00:06:00.590 --> 00:06:04.530
Even today, a good part of the Colombian rainforest
is under the control of this Marxist-Leninist

00:06:04.530 --> 00:06:05.530
group.

00:06:05.530 --> 00:06:10.270
FARC had their own doctors, their own hospitals
and, of course, they collected their own ‘taxes’.

00:06:10.270 --> 00:06:17.909
‘Estimations say this Group has over 20,000
members spread among 24 of the 32 provinces

00:06:17.909 --> 00:06:18.909
Colombia has’

00:06:18.909 --> 00:06:21.430
As you can imagine, FARC were not good friends
of drug trafficking.

00:06:21.430 --> 00:06:26.030
Yes, both, drug traffickers and terrorist
had common enemies... but the idea of becoming

00:06:26.030 --> 00:06:30.240
a millionaire by selling a product on the
international market doesn’t sound very

00:06:30.240 --> 00:06:31.240
Marxist, right?

00:06:31.240 --> 00:06:35.430
Besides, extortion and kidnapping is a very
lucrative business as well, and FARC, well

00:06:35.430 --> 00:06:36.870
they were experts on these matters.

00:06:36.870 --> 00:06:41.830
Add to this the fact that DON BERNA and his
OFICINA de ENVIGADO had an anti-communist

00:06:41.830 --> 00:06:46.750
group on their side and you can imagine the
war that was about to happen...

00:06:46.750 --> 00:06:55.289
‘This is the BOJAYA municipality, today
it’s covered by plants and trees.

00:06:55.289 --> 00:06:59.909
That is the North part, from where FARC launched
the rockets to the other part of the municipality’

00:06:59.909 --> 00:07:01.229
But business is business.

00:07:01.229 --> 00:07:03.850
No matter the money FARC could make with kidnapping…

00:07:03.850 --> 00:07:07.080
it was hard to resist to the temptation of
drug trafficking.

00:07:07.080 --> 00:07:13.620
So one day, MEDINA CARACAS, one of the main
FARC leaders, decided to try the cocaine business.

00:07:13.620 --> 00:07:21.040
‘The 16th front of the FARC, went from 200
members to over 800 thanks to the income of

00:07:21.040 --> 00:07:26.470
the cocaine that became a main source to finance
the guerrillas’

00:07:26.470 --> 00:07:30.930
Don’t forget that FARC had the control of
all the areas where coca plantations where.

00:07:30.930 --> 00:07:33.780
In fact, they had already extorted the growers...

00:07:33.780 --> 00:07:38.530
Nonetheless, with Medina Caracas as leader,
FARC created their own fields and their own

00:07:38.530 --> 00:07:40.610
distribution networks.

00:07:40.610 --> 00:07:42.639
This was all happening by the year 2000.

00:07:42.639 --> 00:07:45.629
At this time, the Cali cartel was already
dismantled.

00:07:45.629 --> 00:07:50.500
But cocaine was still employing a good share
of the Colombian workforce...

00:07:50.500 --> 00:07:58.449
So, to summarise, on one hand, we have the
OFICINA de ENVIGADO with DON BERNA as a leader,

00:07:58.449 --> 00:08:03.150
then we have FARC on the other hand and…
between these two, there was a plethora of

00:08:03.150 --> 00:08:06.479
independent drug trafficking bands called
the BACRIM.

00:08:06.479 --> 00:08:10.740
It was during this time that Colombia chose
a new president, ALVARO URIBE.

00:08:10.740 --> 00:08:15.729
URIBE was born in Medellin and his main political
goal was to end all the violence.

00:08:15.729 --> 00:08:20.300
And this marked the beginning of the…

00:08:20.300 --> 00:08:22.370
PAX MAFIOSA

00:08:22.370 --> 00:08:27.689
Alvaro Uribe was ready to end the guerrilla
warriors and the right wing groups at any

00:08:27.689 --> 00:08:28.689
cost.

00:08:28.689 --> 00:08:33.260
This is why, in the year 2005, his defense
minister, CAMILO OSPINA, signed a law that

00:08:33.260 --> 00:08:35.610
is thought of with sadness in Colombia.

00:08:35.610 --> 00:08:37.190
This was “Directive 029”.

00:08:37.190 --> 00:08:40.330
And now you might be wondering…

00:08:40.330 --> 00:08:43.510
Well, why is that sad?

00:08:43.510 --> 00:08:50.130
This directive said, literally, that the Government
would give the equivalent of $1900 to anyone

00:08:50.130 --> 00:08:56.690
who would murder a guerrilla warrior or a
paramilitary right wing fighter.

00:08:56.690 --> 00:09:02.080
Basically, if you were a soldier in the Colombian
army and you wanted to have a good career,

00:09:02.080 --> 00:09:05.110
all you had to do was get out and go on a
man hunt.

00:09:05.110 --> 00:09:09.660
And all of a sudden, the death toll at FARC
and among narcos, skyrocketed.

00:09:09.660 --> 00:09:13.660
But hold on a minute because this was just
the beginning...

00:09:13.660 --> 00:09:15.860
Finding FARC members was not an easy job.

00:09:15.860 --> 00:09:20.330
But, the reward given by the Colombian government
was really really tempting...

00:09:20.330 --> 00:09:24.130
This is why a lot of soldiers started killing
innocent civilians.

00:09:24.130 --> 00:09:28.580
After that, they would dress them with a FARC
uniform and take a picture of the dead body.

00:09:28.580 --> 00:09:31.900
This was enough to go the the government office
and get the money.

00:09:31.900 --> 00:09:35.020
And this happened more than once or twice.

00:09:35.020 --> 00:09:36.910
There is even a name for it in Colombia.

00:09:36.910 --> 00:09:41.190
The dead civilians were called ‘false positives’
and it became a major way for people to make

00:09:41.190 --> 00:09:42.830
money in Colombia.

00:09:42.830 --> 00:09:48.260
Still today, the Colombian justice system
has over 3000 ongoing cases of ‘false positives’

00:09:48.260 --> 00:09:49.260
that need investigating.

00:09:49.260 --> 00:09:50.750
But, wait a minute…

00:09:50.750 --> 00:09:54.040
The policies of President Uribe were extremely
controversial.

00:09:54.040 --> 00:09:59.600
But one thing has to be said… he made it
way more complicated for FARC guerrilla warriors.

00:09:59.600 --> 00:10:03.290
Raids on cocaine fields and distribution networks
became the norm.

00:10:03.290 --> 00:10:08.130
And when your enemy is killing dozens of your
members, you are willing to sign an alliance

00:10:08.130 --> 00:10:13.580
with the devil himself…

00:10:13.580 --> 00:10:17.920
Some emails prove the links between FARC and
the narcos.

00:10:17.920 --> 00:10:25.400
In one of the messages, EMIRO CONEJO, a guerrilla
leader, shows clear connections with the OFICINA

00:10:25.400 --> 00:10:30.080
DE ENVIGADO.

00:10:30.080 --> 00:10:31.820
&nbsp;
As we said before, FARC weere present at all

00:10:31.820 --> 00:10:33.120
the plantations.

00:10:33.120 --> 00:10:37.900
In some cases, those plantations belonged
to the Oficina de Envigado or some belonged

00:10:37.900 --> 00:10:39.661
to the BACRIM we mentioned earlier.

00:10:39.661 --> 00:10:44.650
On the other hand, some plantations were managed
directly by FARC.

00:10:44.650 --> 00:10:49.200
These are where they grew and processed coca
leaves and turned them into white powder.

00:10:49.200 --> 00:10:53.390
Then, the big cartels stepped in to distribute
the cocaine to countries.

00:10:53.390 --> 00:10:56.040
&nbsp;
Nonetheless, unlike the times of Pablo Escobar,

00:10:56.040 --> 00:11:00.260
Colombian cartels no longer have a monopoly
over distribution.

00:11:00.260 --> 00:11:07.640
For instance, when those Colombian narcos
want to send cocaine to US, they partner with

00:11:07.640 --> 00:11:08.770
Mexican drug dealers.

00:11:08.770 --> 00:11:13.730
When they want to send it to Europe, they
work with Italian, Greek and Albanian mafias.

00:11:13.730 --> 00:11:16.230
But we are going to talk all about that in
another video!

00:11:16.230 --> 00:11:18.483
&nbsp;
The important thing is, despite the fact that

00:11:18.483 --> 00:11:23.080
drug trafficking is still a thing today, Medellin
is now a peaceful city.

00:11:23.080 --> 00:11:26.560
Of course, they still have bad neighbourhoods
where it’s better not to go, especially

00:11:26.560 --> 00:11:28.010
on the outskirts of the city.

00:11:28.010 --> 00:11:29.520
But the city has made a big change.

00:11:29.520 --> 00:11:31.410
A change for better.

00:11:31.410 --> 00:11:33.120
&nbsp;
This ‘pax mafiosa’ has allowed all the

00:11:33.120 --> 00:11:37.760
players involved with the cocaine business
to make an agreement so each of them has their

00:11:37.760 --> 00:11:40.330
territories and they have no reason to kill
each other.

00:11:40.330 --> 00:11:50.940
Yep, now cocaine is easier to find than ever…
but less people die during 

00:11:50.940 --> 00:11:51.940
the process.

00:11:51.940 --> 00:11:52.940
&nbsp;
And now you might be wondering…

00:11:52.940 --> 00:11:56.070
Well, what can will happen now that FARC have
made a peace agreement with the Colombian

00:11:56.070 --> 00:11:57.070
Government?

00:11:57.070 --> 00:12:00.540
Well, this could become an opportunity for
the BACRIM to take back the control of the

00:12:00.540 --> 00:12:03.300
business that is now in the guerrilla's hands...

00:12:03.300 --> 00:12:06.040
But the truth is, those narcos are trying
now to get another peace agreement with the

00:12:06.040 --> 00:12:10.210
government as profitable as the one FARC are
negotiating.

00:12:10.210 --> 00:12:13.000
&nbsp;
Crazy as it sounds, FARC claim to be a political

00:12:13.000 --> 00:12:14.000
group...

00:12:14.000 --> 00:12:15.950
their ideology, their propaganda and even
their website, it’s all politics.

00:12:15.950 --> 00:12:19.710
Their website can be visited by anyone.

00:12:19.710 --> 00:12:22.170
This is why they sit with the government as
equals.

00:12:22.170 --> 00:12:27.560
However, the BACRIM are seen as ordinary criminals,
with no politics or ideology whatsoever…

00:12:27.560 --> 00:12:30.350
&nbsp;
And, of course, those narcos are wondering…

00:12:30.350 --> 00:12:33.160
Why can FARC can talk with the government
and we can’t?

00:12:33.160 --> 00:12:36.960
The agreements between FARC and the government
are extremely good for the guerrillas.

00:12:36.960 --> 00:12:47.170
And, once again, everyone wants a piece 
of the cake.

00:12:47.170 --> 00:12:48.210
&nbsp;
But… that’s another story.

00:12:48.210 --> 00:12:49.260
Now it is your turn.

00:12:49.260 --> 00:12:52.310
Do you think it is possible to end the trafficking
of cocaine?

00:12:52.310 --> 00:12:56.860
Or do you think it’s a matter that each
time a band is dismantled, a new one appears?

00:12:56.860 --> 00:13:01.220
Well, please, leave your answers in the comments
section below.

